 ],
 "notes": "No PROMPT_GT_MISMATCH. The adapter resolves variables with non-null defaults into __declared__ properties, so a variable-driven setting cannot be told apart from a literal; 'accepts parameters' is therefore checked as either a var/local reference or a variable whose name states the setting. force_destroy is read from the declared bucket plus a 'force' variable defaulting to false (the planned false is the provider default and proves nothing). Statement fields are bound to the policy document the bucket policy references (an unrelated KMS key policy document no longer counts), or to an inline jsonencode policy. The Effect default of Allow lives in the variable's type constraint, which the normaliser does not expose, so only the presence of an effect field is checked. A template that passes raw policy JSON through from a variable (no document built) fails the statement-field details by design. 23 checks is above the L2 norm because the prompt enumerates each policy-object field separately."
}